meta {
  name: Concat - Basic URL Response
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/concat?response_mode=url
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  response_mode: url
}

body:json {
  {
    "files": [
      "concatenation_test/01-sarah-audio.mp3",
      "concatenation_test/02-mark-audio.mp3",
      "concatenation_test/03-sarah-audio.mp3"
    ],
    "export_formats": ["wav", "mp3"],
    "normalize_levels": true
  }
}

docs {
  # Audio Concatenation - Basic URL Response
  
  Returns JSON metadata instead of streaming the file directly. Best for workflows needing file information.
  
  ## Input Method
  - **Content-Type**: application/json
  - **Files**: Must exist in outputs/ directory
  
  ## Response Mode
  - **response_mode=url**: Returns JSON with file URLs and metadata
  - Includes processing information, duration, and file details
  
  ## Parameters
  - Same as Basic Stream Response (see Concat - Basic Stream Response.bru)
  
  ## Response
  ```json
  {
    "output_files": ["concat_2025-10-29_123456_789012_3files_leveled.wav", "concat_2025-10-29_123456_789012_3files_leveled.mp3"],
    "generation_info": {
      "total_duration_seconds": 45.2,
      "file_count": 3,
      "processing_time_seconds": 1.8,
      "processing_details": [
        {
          "type": "file",
          "filename": "01-sarah-audio.mp3",
          "duration_seconds": 15.0
        },
        {
          "type": "file",
          "filename": "02-mark-audio.mp3",
          "duration_seconds": 15.1
        },
        {
          "type": "file",
          "filename": "03-sarah-audio.mp3",
          "duration_seconds": 15.1
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example Use Case
  - Web applications needing file information
  - Batch processing workflows
  - API integrations requiring metadata
  - Async processing confirmations
}
